{"requirements":[],"conflicts":[],"gaps":[{"title":"Responsibility for cross-emirate clinical coordination","type":"no_provision_found","description":"There is no provision in the provided texts that explicitly assigns responsibility for coordinating clinical follow-up or medication safety responses between healthcare facilities located in different emirates (e.g., Abu Dhabi and Dubai). While policies emphasize sectoral coordination and the importance of health information exchange for continuity of care, they do not define the specific clinical governance or accountability mechanisms for multi-prescriber, cross-emirate scenarios.","citations":[],"recommendation":"Consult the relevant health authorities (DoH Abu Dhabi and DHA Dubai) for guidance on cross-emirate clinical governance and patient safety protocols."},{"title":"Impact of patient-withheld data on clinical responsibility","type":"no_provision_found","description":"The provided texts do not specify how a patient's choice to withhold data from a health information exchange (such as NABIDH) affects the clinical responsibility or duty of care of a provider who is unable to access that data for safety assessments.","citations":[],"recommendation":"Review institutional policies regarding the management of incomplete clinical records and the legal implications of patient-imposed data access restrictions."}],"comparisons":[{"statement":"EU regulations (EHDS) establish that importers of EHR systems must investigate complaints and follow up on information received regarding incidents involving their systems, keeping relevant parties informed.","citations":["eu-ehds-2025-327#0128"]},{"statement":"EU regulations (EHDS) note that when natural persons restrict access to their health data, they should assume responsibility for the fact that the healthcare provider cannot take that data into account when providing health services, though access should remain possible in emergency situations to protect vital interests.","citations":["eu-ehds-2025-327#0010"]}],"caveats":["The provided policies focus on the technical and regulatory framework for health information exchange (ADHIE) and data management, rather than clinical decision-making or cross-emirate care coordination protocols.","The inability to access data due to patient choice is a significant limitation that is not addressed by the current regulatory excerpts provided."]}
